RSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;6 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;3&lt;br&gt;Automation-grade Anki CLI for safe, local-first collection management, study flows, and agent use.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/officewizards/officewizards-agent-skills&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;officewizards-agent-skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;1 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;1&lt;br&gt;Office Wizards agent skills and plugin manifests.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Hi, I&#39;m Tak&lt;/h1&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I build agent-first software, learning tools, and developer tooling.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I am currently focused on software that humans install and supervise, but agents can operate directly through strong CLI surfaces, structured output, and safe automation workflows.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Current Projects&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Takhoffman/ankicli&quot;&gt;ankicli&lt;/a&gt; - agent-first Anki CLI for studying, card authoring, deck management, media workflows, and automation.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Takhoffman/winmote&quot;&gt;winmote&lt;/a&gt; - remote control and automation tooling for Windows workflows.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Takhoffman/agent-scripts&quot;&gt;agent-scripts&lt;/a&gt; - reusable automation and maintainer scripts for agent-driven workflows.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What I Like Building&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;agent-operated software&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;learning systems&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;CLI-first products&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;automation-heavy developer tools&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;local-first workflows with clear safety boundaries&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Current Direction&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Right now I am especially interested in a new era of software where:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;humans choose the tools, install them, and set the constraints&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;agents operate the software directly&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;the product surface is designed for both supervision and execution&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;That shows up in my work as structured CLIs, installable skills, automation primitives, and products that are easy to hand off to an agent harness without losing control.&lt;/p&gt; 
